+++ b/HANDOFF-air-sports.md
@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+# HANDOFF: air sports (phase 3 of the hill content, package P)
+
+Parachuting (helicopter bails, the BASE exit) and the bungee jump.
+Decisions note of package P; the task's note is HANDOFF-hill-content.md.
+
+## Files
+
+- `game/scripts/parachute.gd`: free fall, canopy, landing, BASE exit.
+- `game/scripts/bungee.gd`: jump arm site, rope-spring jump, winch.
+- `game/scripts/kits/air_sports_kit.gd`: canopy + lines, risers, BASE
+  plank/windsock/board, jump arm (truss, mast, stays), rope.
+- `game/scripts/player.gd`: `air`, `flies`, `above_land`; `air.drive()`
+  replaces the walk while set; `_chute_bail()` in `exit_vehicle`;
+  `_air_sport_interact()` on E; `air.cancel()` in `respawn`/`stand_at`.
+- `game/tests/air_sports_tests.gd` (7 tests), `tests/air_sports_shots.tscn`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Both nodes join group `air_sports` (player.gd's E reaches them without
+  main.gd); the parachute also joins `parachute` (player.gd's bail looks it
+  up). No parachute node = old fall everywhere.
+- MIN_HEIGHT 40 m over the ground (Terrain.height - drop) at the bail.
+  Below it, player.gd's fall is untouched. Killed in the air: hand the body
+  to player.gd's fall (`_hand_to_fall`).
+- Free fall: quadratic drag, terminal 50 m/s; stick tracks up to 12 m/s.
+  OPEN (E) any time; auto-open at `open_height(v)` = 32 m + the distance
+  the 0.6 s line stretch and the 0.6 s braking take, so the canopy is fully
+  flying about 32 m up. Canopy: 5 m/s down, 8 m/s ahead, stick turns it
+  (1.4 rad/s), E brakes 2 s (3 down, 4 ahead), flare under 4 m (1.2 down,
+  3 ahead). Landing damage uses player.gd's formula on the impact's
+  equivalent drop (v²/2g): 7 m/s or less costs nothing; > 2.5 m/s stumbles.
+- Canopy landings on a roof or in water move to open dry ground nearby
+  (`_open_ground_near`, as the helicopter's).
+- BASE exit: best lip within 40 m of (1035, -2740): level behind, ≥ 8 m
+  down in 8 m, ≥ 20 in 16, ≥ 45 in 64. Found at (1056, 981, -2720), facing
+  east, 70 m down in 64 m. The jump throws the canopy at once (no free
+  fall: the ground is right there).
+- Bungee: the hillside by the pad falls about 1.5 m per metre (8 m terrain
+  grid, no sheer cliff); a 20 m arm hung only 35 m up, and a cliff with
+  ≥ 60 m of drop is 215 m away (and still needs a 30 m arm). So the arm is a
+  long jib from the pad edge: the shortest of 12-40 m that hangs WANT_DROP
+  (60 m) over the highest ground within 2.5 m of the tip. Found: root
+  (721, 900, -2723), 36 m long, 60 m drop. Price $60.
+- Rope from the measured drop: reach = drop - BODY 2.6 - CLEAR 3 - MARGIN
+  1; slack l0 = 0.42 reach; stiffness from energy (undamped the ankles
+  just reach `reach`); damping 0.12 of critical, air drag. Ends after 4
+  lows (or 30 s), winch at up to 4 m/s, flip onto the catwalk, walk back.
+- Sites are measured once when the player comes within 1200 m (well
+  before the country's tiles there build, so the clearings keep trees off
+  the arm and the plank). Cost: about 40 ms (BASE) and 70-150 ms (arm).
+- Ground for landings: `Parachute.ground_under(x, z)` = Terrain.height -
+  Terrain.drop. **Switch it to Ground.height(x, z, y_hint) when package G
+  lands** (one function; bungee.gd's walk-down uses it too).
+
+## Traps
+
+- player.gd's `_physics_process` returns before `super()` while `air` is
+  set: humanoid physics, knock-down timers and the ground snap do not run.
+  `_release()` restores layers, rotation and `_drop_at`.
+- The camera on foot follows the stick only when `player.velocity` moves:
+  the flight keeps its own `velocity`, so the view holds still while
+  steering (world_move stays consistent).
+
+## Patches for the main session
+
+See the package report (main.gd, hud.gd). camera.gd: none needed.
+
+## Open items
+
+- The lot's name says "129 m drop"; the jump is 60 m (data not regenerated).
diff --git a/game/scripts/bungee.gd b/game/scripts/bungee.gd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..65ad140
--- /dev/null
+++ b/game/scripts/bungee.gd
@@ -0,0 +1,467 @@
+extends Node
+## The bungee jump at the Calder platform lot (HANDOFF-air-sports.md). The
+## lot sits on a level pad, so a steel jump arm reaches out from the pad's
+## edge over the steepest drop beside it, found from the terrain at run
+## time. E at the arm's steps (PRICE taken) walks the player out, a swan
+## dive off the tip, a rope-spring fall with decaying bounces, the winch
+## back up and a walk back. The rope is cut from the measured drop so the
+## lowest the body reaches stays CLEAR m or more over the ground under it.
+## While jumping this node drives the player (player.air), as parachute.gd.
+##
+## main.gd: `bungee = Bungee.new(); bungee.game = self; add_child(bungee)`.
+
+const Kit = preload("res://scripts/kits/air_sports_kit.gd")
+const MeshBuilder = preload("res://scripts/mesh_builder.gd")
+const Terrain = preload("res://scripts/terrain.gd")
+const GameLog = preload("res://scripts/game_log.gd")
+const Parachute = preload("res://scripts/parachute.gd")
+const Tiles = preload("res://scripts/country_tiles.gd")
+
+const LOT_ID := "calder_bungee"
+## The lot's centre, when the country data has no such lot.
+const LOT := Vector2(746.14, -2708.86)
+const PRICE := 60
+## The arm: from level ground within ROOT_R m of the lot (within PAD_LEVEL m
+## of its height), ARM_MIN to ARM_MAX m long (ARM_STEP apart in the search),
+## its catwalk DECK_H m up. The pad's hillside falls about 1.5 m a metre
+## (no sheer cliff on an 8 m terrain grid), so the arm is a long jib: the
+## shortest that hangs WANT_DROP m over the ground wins; short of that each
+## metre of drop is worth DROP_WORTH m of arm.
+const ROOT_R := 45.0
+const PAD_LEVEL := 1.5
+const ARM_MIN := 12
+const ARM_MAX := 40
+const ARM_STEP := 4
+const WANT_DROP := 60.0
+const DROP_WORTH := 2.0
+const DECK_H := 0.8
+## The rope: hanging head down the body reaches BODY m under the ankles; the
+## lowest point keeps CLEAR m over the highest ground near the tip, with
+## MARGIN to spare. The rope's slack is RATIO of the fall to that point;
+## its damping ZETA of critical; AIR and HDAMP are the air's drag.
+const BODY := 2.6
+const CLEAR := 3.0
+const MARGIN := 1.0
+const RATIO := 0.42
+const ZETA := 0.12
+const AIR := 0.004
+const HDAMP := 0.4
+const MIN_FALL := 10.0
+## The dive: out and up off the tip (m/s).
+const DIVE_OUT := 0.7
+const DIVE_UP := 1.5
+const DIVE_TIME := 1.2
+## Walking the catwalk, the winch, the prompt's reach (m from the steps).
+const WALK := 3.5
+const WINCH := 4.0
+const REACH := 3.0
+## The jump ends after LOWS low points, or MAX_TIME s on the rope.
+const LOWS := 4
+const MAX_TIME := 30.0
+## The site is measured this close to the lot (see parachute.gd).
+const PREPARE_RANGE := 1200.0
+const G := 9.8
+
+var game
+## "" (not jumping), "climb", "walk_out", "ready", "fall", "winch", "flip",
+## "walk_back", "down".
+var state := ""
+var player = null
+## Each low and high of the ankles on the rope, metres from the anchor (up +).
+var lows: Array = []
+var highs: Array = []
+## The lowest the body came over the ground under it in this jump (m).
+var lowest_clear := INF
+var _site := {}
+var _site_done := false
+var _prepare_tick := 0.0
+var _t := 0.0
+var _p := Vector3.ZERO
+var _v := Vector3.ZERO
+var _from := Vector3.ZERO
+var _arm: MeshInstance3D
+var _rope: MeshInstance3D
+
+
+func _ready() -> void:
+	if game == null:
+		game = get_parent()
+	add_to_group("air_sports")
+	add_to_group("bungee")
+	_rope = MeshInstance3D.new()
+	_rope.name = "BungeeRope"
+	_rope.mesh = Kit.rope()
+	_rope.material_override = MeshBuilder.material()
+	_rope.physics_interpolation_mode = Node.PHYSICS_INTERPOLATION_MODE_OFF
+	_rope.visible = false
+	add_child(_rope)
+
+
+func _process(delta: float) -> void:
+	_prepare_tick -= delta
+	if not _site_done and _prepare_tick <= 0.0:
+		_prepare_tick = 0.5
+		var p = game.get("player") if game != null else null
+		if p != null and Vector2(p.global_position.x, p.global_position.z).distance_to(_lot()) < PREPARE_RANGE:
+			site()
+	if player != null and state in ["ready", "fall", "winch"]:
+		var feet: Vector3 = player.get_global_transform_interpolated().origin
+		var eye := _anchor() + Vector3(0.0, -0.35, 0.0)
+		_rope.global_transform = Transform3D(Kit.along(eye, feet), eye)
+		_rope.visible = true
+	else:
+		_rope.visible = false
+
+
+func _lot() -> Vector2:
+	var city = game.get("city") if game != null else null
+	var country = city.get("country") if city != null else null
+	if country != null:
+		var lm: Dictionary = country.landmark(LOT_ID)
+		if not lm.is_empty():
+			return Vector2(lm.pos.x, lm.pos.z)
+	return LOT
+
+
+# --- The site -----------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## The jump arm and its rope, measured from the terrain once: root (on the
+## ground), dir (out along the arm), length, deck (catwalk height), tip (at
+## the catwalk), drop (catwalk to the highest ground near the tip), the
+## rope's slack l0, stiffness k and damping c (per kg). {} if no drop will do.
+func site() -> Dictionary:
+	if _site_done:
+		return _site
+	_site_done = true
+	if Terrain.nx == 0:
+		return _site
+	var lot := _lot()
+	var pad := Terrain.height(lot.x, lot.y)
+	var best := [-INF, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0]
+	var x := lot.x - ROOT_R
+	while x <= lot.x + ROOT_R:
+		var z := lot.y - ROOT_R
+		while z <= lot.y + ROOT_R:
+			if Vector2(x, z).distance_to(lot) <= ROOT_R and _root_ok(x, z, pad):
+				for a in 24:
+					best = _better_arm(best, x, z, TAU * a / 24.0, ARM_MIN, ARM_MAX, ARM_STEP, lot)
+			z += 4.0
+		x += 4.0
+	if best[0] == -INF:
+		return _site
+	var bx: float = best[1]
+	var bz: float = best[2]
+	var ba: float = best[3]
+	var bl: int = best[4]
+	for i in range(-3, 4):
+		for j in range(-3, 4):
+			if not _root_ok(bx + i, bz + j, pad) or Vector2(bx + i, bz + j).distance_to(lot) > ROOT_R + 4.0:
+				continue
+			for k in range(-3, 4):
+				best = _better_arm(best, bx + i, bz + j, ba + deg_to_rad(2.5 * k), maxi(ARM_MIN, bl - ARM_STEP),
+						mini(ARM_MAX, bl + ARM_STEP), 1, lot)
+	var dir := Vector3(cos(best[3]), 0.0, sin(best[3]))
+	var root := Vector3(best[1], 0.0, best[2])
+	root.y = Terrain.height(root.x, root.z)
+	var length: float = best[4]
+	var deck := root.y + DECK_H
+	var tip := root + dir * length
+	tip.y = deck
+	var drop := deck - _highest_near(tip.x, tip.z)
+	# The rope: undamped, the ankles would just reach `reach` under the
+	# anchor; the body then hangs BODY under them, CLEAR + MARGIN up.
+	var reach := drop - BODY - CLEAR - MARGIN
+	if reach < MIN_FALL:
+		return _site
+	var l0 := RATIO * reach
+	var stretch := reach - l0
+	var rise := DIVE_UP * DIVE_UP / (2.0 * G)
+	var k := 2.0 * G * (reach + rise) / (stretch * stretch)
+	_site = {"root": root, "dir": dir, "length": length, "deck": deck, "tip": tip, "drop": drop,
+			"l0": l0, "k": k, "c": ZETA * 2.0 * sqrt(k), "gate": root - dir * 2.6}
+	_build_arm()
+	return _site
+
+
+static func _root_ok(x: float, z: float, pad: float) -> bool:
+	return absf(Terrain.height(x, z) - pad) <= PAD_LEVEL and Terrain.normal(x, z).y >= 0.85
+
+
+## `best` or an arm from (x, z) toward `ang`, `from` to `to` m long
+## (`step` apart), if one scores higher: the drop (up to WANT_DROP), a short
+## arm, near the lot. A longer arm than one the ground blocks is blocked
+## too, and one longer than the first that reaches WANT_DROP only costs more.
+static func _better_arm(best: Array, x: float, z: float, ang: float, from: int, to: int, step: int, lot: Vector2) -> Array:
+	var near := 0.2 * Vector2(x, z).distance_to(lot)
+	var l := from
+	while l <= to:
+		var d := _arm_drop(x, z, ang, l)
+		if d == -INF:
+			break
+		var s := minf(d, WANT_DROP) * DROP_WORTH - l - near
+		if s > best[0]:
+			best = [s, x, z, ang, l]
+		if d >= WANT_DROP:
+			break
+		l += step
+	return best
+
+
+## The drop from the catwalk at the tip of an arm from (x, z) toward `ang`,
+## `l` m long, or -INF when the ground along it comes up under the catwalk.
+static func _arm_drop(x: float, z: float, ang: float, l: int) -> float:
+	var dx := cos(ang)
+	var dz := sin(ang)
+	var deck := Terrain.height(x, z) + DECK_H
+	var s := 2
+	while s <= l:
+		if Terrain.height(x + dx * s, z + dz * s) > deck - 0.3:
+			return -INF
+		s += 2
+	return deck - _highest_near(x + dx * l, z + dz * l)
+
+
+## The highest ground within 2.5 m of (x, z): where a swinging body could reach.
+static func _highest_near(x: float, z: float) -> float:
+	var m := Terrain.height(x, z)
+	for a in 8:
+		var ang := TAU * a / 8.0
+		m = maxf(m, Terrain.height(x + cos(ang) * 2.5, z + sin(ang) * 2.5))
+	return m
+
+
+func _build_arm() -> void:
+	var root: Vector3 = _site.root
+	var dir: Vector3 = _site.dir
+	var length: float = _site.length
+	var yaw := atan2(-dir.x, -dir.z)
+	var back := root - dir * 9.0
+	_arm = MeshInstance3D.new()
+	_arm.name = "BungeeArm"
+	_arm.mesh = Kit.jump_arm(length, DECK_H, Terrain.height(back.x, back.z) - root.y)
+	_arm.material_override = MeshBuilder.material()
+	add_child(_arm)
+	_arm.global_transform = Transform3D(Basis(Vector3.UP, yaw), root)
+	# No trees along the arm or in the fall under its tip.
+	var mid := root + dir * (length * 0.5 - 2.0)
+	Tiles.clearings.append([Vector2(mid.x, mid.z), yaw, Vector2(3.0, length * 0.5 + 9.0)])
+	Tiles.clearings.append([Vector2(_site.tip.x, _site.tip.z), yaw, Vector2(6.0, 6.0)])
+
+
+func _anchor() -> Vector3:
+	return _site.tip if not _site.is_empty() else Vector3.ZERO
+
+
+# --- The HUD and E ------------------------------------------------------------
+
+func _at_gate() -> bool:
+	var p = game.get("player") if game != null else null
+	if p == null or p.vehicle != null or p.dead or p.knocked_time > 0.0 or p.air != null or not p.controllable:
+		return false
+	if Vector2(p.global_position.x, p.global_position.z).distance_to(_lot()) > ROOT_R + 30.0:
+		return false
+	var s := site()
+	if s.is_empty():
+		return false
+	var at: Vector3 = s.gate
+	return Vector2(p.global_position.x - at.x, p.global_position.z - at.z).length() <= REACH
+
+
+## [text, button] for the HUD: the offer at the arm's steps, or how the
+## jump goes; [] otherwise.
+func prompt() -> Array:
+	if state != "":
+		match state:
+			"fall":
+				return ["Bungee   %d m drop" % roundi(_site.drop), "JUMP"]
+			"winch":
+				return ["Bungee   winching you up", "JUMP"]
+		return ["Bungee", "JUMP"]
+	if _at_gate():
+		return ["Bungee: E ($%d)" % PRICE, "JUMP"]
+	return []
+
+
+## At the steps: pays and jumps, or says what it costs. True when it took E.
+func try_interact() -> bool:
+	if state != "" or not _at_gate():
+		return false
+	if game.cash < PRICE:
+		if game.hud != null:
+			game.hud.show_message("A bungee jump costs $%d" % PRICE)
+		GameLog.event("bungee_refused", {"cash": game.cash})
+		return true
+	game.cash -= PRICE
+	_start(game.player)
+	return true
+
+
+func _start(p) -> void:
+	player = p
+	p.air = self
+	state = "climb"
+	_t = 0.0
+	lows = []
+	highs = []
+	lowest_clear = INF
+	_from = p.global_position
+	p.velocity = Vector3.ZERO
+	p.collision_layer = 0
+	p.collision_mask = 0
+	var dir: Vector3 = _site.dir
+	p.rotation.y = atan2(-dir.x, -dir.z)
+	GameLog.event("bungee_jump", {"drop": _site.drop, "l0": _site.l0, "k": _site.k})
+
+
+# --- The jump -----------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## One physics frame of the jump (player.gd calls this while p.air is us).
+func drive(p, delta: float) -> void:
+	if p.dead:
+		_hand_to_fall(p)
+		return
+	_t += delta
+	var dir: Vector3 = _site.dir
+	var root: Vector3 = _site.root
+	var deck: float = _site.deck
+	var on_deck := Vector3(root.x, deck, root.z)
+	var tip_stand: Vector3 = _site.tip - dir * 0.3
+	match state:
+		"climb":
+			var k := smoothstep(0.0, 1.0, minf(_t / 0.8, 1.0))
+			p.global_position = _from.lerp(on_deck, k)
+			p.velocity = dir * WALK * 0.6
+			if _t >= 0.8:
+				_next("walk_out")
+		"walk_out":
+			p.global_position = p.global_position.move_toward(tip_stand, WALK * delta)
+			p.velocity = dir * WALK
+			if p.global_position.distance_to(tip_stand) < 0.01:
+				p.velocity = Vector3.ZERO
+				p.gesture = "hands_up"
+				p.flies = true
+				p.above_land = _site.drop
+				_next("ready")
+		"ready":
+			if _t >= 1.0:
+				_p = p.global_position
+				_v = dir * DIVE_OUT + Vector3.UP * DIVE_UP
+				_next("fall")
+		"fall":
+			p.rotation.x = -PI * smoothstep(0.0, 1.0, minf(_t / DIVE_TIME, 1.0))
+			_rope_step(delta)
+			p.global_position = _p
+			if lows.size() >= LOWS or _t > MAX_TIME:
+				_next("winch")
+		"winch":
+			_v = Vector3.ZERO
+			var top := _anchor() + Vector3(0.0, -1.2, 0.0)
+			_p = _p.move_toward(top, minf(WINCH, 0.5 + _t * 2.0) * delta)
+			p.global_position = _p
+			if _p.distance_to(top) < 0.01:
+				_p = top
+				_next("flip")
+		"flip":
+			var k := smoothstep(0.0, 1.0, minf(_t / 1.0, 1.0))
+			var top := _anchor() + Vector3(0.0, -1.2, 0.0)
+			p.global_position = top.lerp(tip_stand, k) + Vector3.UP * sin(k * PI) * 0.4
+			p.rotation.x = lerpf(-PI, 0.0, k)
+			if _t >= 1.0:
+				p.rotation.x = 0.0
+				p.gesture = ""
+				p.flies = false
+				p.above_land = 0.0
+				p.rotation.y = atan2(dir.x, dir.z)
+				_next("walk_back")
+		"walk_back":
+			p.global_position = p.global_position.move_toward(on_deck, WALK * delta)
+			p.velocity = -dir * WALK
+			if p.global_position.distance_to(on_deck) < 0.01:
+				_from = on_deck
+				_next("down")
+		"down":
+			var k := smoothstep(0.0, 1.0, minf(_t / 0.8, 1.0))
+			var gate: Vector3 = _site.gate
+			gate.y = Parachute.ground_under(gate.x, gate.z)
+			p.global_position = _from.lerp(gate, k)
+			p.velocity = -dir * WALK * 0.6
+			if _t >= 0.8:
+				_finish(p)
+				return
+	_track_clearance(p)
+
+
+func _next(s: String) -> void:
+	state = s
+	_t = 0.0
+
+
+## The rope and the air on the jumper (the ankles, at _p): gravity, the
+## rope's spring and damping while it is stretched and pulling, drag.
+func _rope_step(delta: float) -> void:
+	var anchor := _anchor()
+	var a := Vector3(0.0, -G, 0.0) - _v * _v.length() * AIR
+	a.x -= _v.x * HDAMP
+	a.z -= _v.z * HDAMP
+	var r := _p - anchor
+	var d := r.length()
+	var l0: float = _site.l0
+	if d > l0:
+		var u := r / d
+		var f: float = _site.k * (d - l0) + _site.c * _v.dot(u)
+		if f > 0.0:
+			a -= u * f
+	var vy_was := _v.y
+	_v += a * delta
+	_p += _v * delta
+	if vy_was < 0.0 and _v.y >= 0.0:
+		lows.append(_p.y - anchor.y)
+	elif vy_was > 0.0 and _v.y <= 0.0 and _t > 0.5:
+		highs.append(_p.y - anchor.y)
+
+
+## On the rope: the lowest the body (BODY under the ankles) has come over
+## the ground, and the height over the land the camera reads.
+func _track_clearance(p) -> void:
+	if state in ["fall", "winch"]:
+		var feet: Vector3 = p.global_position
+		lowest_clear = minf(lowest_clear, feet.y - BODY - Terrain.height(feet.x, feet.z))
+		p.above_land = maxf(feet.y - Parachute.ground_under(feet.x, feet.z), 0.0)
+
+
+func _finish(p) -> void:
+	GameLog.event("bungee_done", {"lows": lows, "lowest_clear": lowest_clear})
+	_release(p)
+
+
+func _release(p) -> void:
+	state = ""
+	player = null
+	p.air = null
+	p.flies = false
+	p.above_land = 0.0
+	p.gesture = ""
+	p.rotation.x = 0.0
+	p.rotation.z = 0.0
+	p.velocity = Vector3.ZERO
+	if not p.dead:
+		p._set_standing_layers()
+	p.set("_drop_at", Vector2.INF)
+	p.reset_physics_interpolation()
+
+
+## Killed on the rope: player.gd's fall takes the body down.
+func _hand_to_fall(p) -> void:
+	var pos: Vector3 = p.global_position
+	var h := maxf(pos.y - Parachute.ground_under(pos.x, pos.z), 0.0)
+	_release(p)
+	p._fall = h
+	p._fall_v = 0.0
+	p._fall_from = h
+
+
+## Ends the jump at once (player.gd's stand_at and respawn).
+func cancel() -> void:
+	if player != null:
+		_release(player)
+	state = ""
diff --git a/game/scripts/kits/air_sports_kit.gd b/game/scripts/kits/air_sports_kit.gd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..46822ec
--- /dev/null
+++ b/game/scripts/kits/air_sports_kit.gd
@@ -0,0 +1,220 @@
+extends RefCounted
+## Meshes for the air sports (parachute.gd, bungee.gd): the canopy and its
+## lines, the risers, the BASE exit's plank and windsock, the bungee jump
+## arm and its rope. All original, low-poly, vertex-coloured.
+
+const MeshBuilder = preload("res://scripts/mesh_builder.gd")
+
+## The canopy: CELLS cells across SPAN m on an arc, CHORD m deep; its lowest
+## edge sits LINE_RISE m over the riser point (where the lines meet).
+const CELLS := 8
+const SPAN := 7.2
+const CHORD := 2.6
+const ARC := 0.7 # half the arc's angle (rad)
+const LINE_RISE := 4.4
+## Where the lines meet, over the feet (the harness hangs under it).
+const RISER_Y := 2.3
+const SHOULDER_Y := 1.45
+
+const TEAL := Color(0.06, 0.42, 0.47)
+const SUN := Color(0.97, 0.76, 0.2)
+const CORAL := Color(0.9, 0.36, 0.3)
+const LINE := Color(0.88, 0.88, 0.84)
+const STEEL := Color(0.86, 0.33, 0.12)
+const STEEL_DK := Color(0.32, 0.31, 0.3)
+const GRATE := Color(0.46, 0.46, 0.44)
+const TIMBER := Color(0.55, 0.4, 0.24)
+const CONCRETE := Color(0.62, 0.61, 0.58)
+const ROPE := Color(0.95, 0.42, 0.18)
+
+static var _cloth: StandardMaterial3D
+
+
+## Both faces drawn: the canopy is seen from above and, swinging, its
+## underside.
+static func cloth_material() -> StandardMaterial3D:
+	if _cloth == null:
+		_cloth = MeshBuilder.material().duplicate()
+		_cloth.cull_mode = BaseMaterial3D.CULL_DISABLED
+	return _cloth
+
+
+## The airfoil section across a cell: [z, y] from the nose round the top
+## and back under it.
+static func _section() -> Array:
+	var h := CHORD * 0.5
+	return [Vector2(-h, 0.0), Vector2(-h * 0.45, 0.34), Vector2(h * 0.3, 0.22), Vector2(h, 0.04),
+		Vector2(h * 0.3, -0.04), Vector2(-h * 0.45, -0.08)]
+
+
+## A point of the wing: rib `phi` (rad across the arc), section point `s`;
+## the riser point is the origin.
+static func _wing_point(phi: float, s: Vector2) -> Vector3:
+	var r := SPAN * 0.5 / sin(ARC)
+	# The arc's centre, so the wing tips sit LINE_RISE over the risers.
+	var centre_y := LINE_RISE - r * cos(ARC)
+	var rr := r + s.y
+	return Vector3(rr * sin(phi), centre_y + rr * cos(phi), s.x)
+
+
+## The canopy and its lines, the riser point at the origin (scale it about
+## there to inflate). Up is +y, ahead is -z.
+static func canopy() -> ArrayMesh:
+	var mb := MeshBuilder.new()
+	var sec := _section()
+	var ribs: Array = []
+	for i in CELLS + 1:
+		ribs.append(lerpf(-ARC, ARC, float(i) / CELLS))
+	for i in CELLS:
+		var mid := absf(i - (CELLS - 1) * 0.5) < 1.0
+		var top: Color = CORAL if mid else (TEAL if i % 2 == 0 else SUN)
+		var under := top.darkened(0.3)
+		var a: float = ribs[i]
+		var b: float = ribs[i + 1]
+		var out := Vector3(sin((a + b) * 0.5), cos((a + b) * 0.5), 0.0)
+		for k in sec.size():
+			var s0: Vector2 = sec[k]
+			var s1: Vector2 = sec[(k + 1) % sec.size()]
+			var upper := k < 3
+			var n := out if upper else -out
+			if k == sec.size() - 1:
+				n = Vector3(0, 0, -1) # the open nose
+			mb.quad(_wing_point(a, s0), _wing_point(b, s0), _wing_point(b, s1), _wing_point(a, s1), n,
+					top if upper else under)
+	# Rib walls at the cells' sides, a shade darker than the cloth.
+	for i in CELLS + 1:
+		var phi: float = ribs[i]
+		var side := Vector3(cos(phi), -sin(phi), 0.0)
+		var c := _wing_point(phi, Vector2(0, 0.08))
+		for k in sec.size():
+			var s0: Vector2 = sec[k]
+			var s1: Vector2 = sec[(k + 1) % sec.size()]
+			mb.tri(c, _wing_point(phi, s0), _wing_point(phi, s1), side, TEAL.darkened(0.45))
+	# Lines: from three points under each rib to the two riser points.
+	var h := CHORD * 0.5
+	for i in CELLS + 1:
+		var phi: float = ribs[i]
+		var riser := Vector3(signf(phi) * 0.25 if absf(phi) > 0.01 else 0.0, 0.0, 0.0)
+		for z: float in [-h * 0.6, 0.0, h * 0.6]:
+			var p := _wing_point(phi, Vector2(z, -0.06))
+			mb.limb(riser, p, 0.018, 0.018, LINE, 3, false)
+	return mb.commit()
+
+
+## The risers and harness straps from the line ends down to the shoulders,
+## the feet at the origin.
+static func risers() -> ArrayMesh:
+	var mb := MeshBuilder.new()
+	for s: float in [-1.0, 1.0]:
+		mb.limb(Vector3(s * 0.25, RISER_Y, 0.0), Vector3(s * 0.2, SHOULDER_Y, 0.04), 0.03, 0.03, STEEL_DK, 4, false)
+		# The toggles the hands hold.
+		mb.box(Vector3(s * 0.32, RISER_Y - 0.15, 0.0), Vector3(0.05, 0.16, 0.05), CORAL)
+	return mb.commit()
+
+
+## The BASE exit at a lip: a timber plank jutting over the edge, two
+## orange posts, a windsock and a striped board. The lip is the origin, the
+## drop ahead (-z); `back_y` is the ground 2 m behind, relative.
+static func base_exit(back_y: float) -> ArrayMesh:
+	var mb := MeshBuilder.new()
+	mb.box(Vector3(0.0, 0.06, -0.2), Vector3(0.7, 0.08, 2.6), TIMBER)
+	for z: float in [-0.9, 0.3, 0.9]:
+		mb.box(Vector3(0.0, 0.03, z), Vector3(0.82, 0.06, 0.12), TIMBER.darkened(0.25))
+	for s: float in [-1.0, 1.0]:
+		mb.cylinder(Vector3(s * 0.45, back_y - 0.2, 1.2), 0.06, 1.3 - back_y, CORAL, 6)
+	# Windsock on a pole off to the side, pointing along the slope.
+	var pole := Vector3(2.4, back_y, 1.6)
+	mb.cylinder(pole + Vector3(0, -0.2, 0), 0.05, 4.0, STEEL_DK, 6)
+	for k in 4:
+		var a := pole + Vector3(0.1 + k * 0.3, 3.6 - k * 0.06, -0.05 - k * 0.12)
+		var b := pole + Vector3(0.1 + (k + 1) * 0.3, 3.6 - (k + 1) * 0.06, -0.05 - (k + 1) * 0.12)
+		mb.limb(a, b, 0.26 - k * 0.04, 0.22 - k * 0.04, CORAL if k % 2 == 0 else Color(0.96, 0.95, 0.92), 8, k == 3)
+	# A board on two legs behind the plank: yellow with dark chevrons.
+	var bp := Vector3(-1.6, back_y, 2.2)
+	for s: float in [-1.0, 1.0]:
+		mb.cylinder(bp + Vector3(s * 0.45, -0.2, 0), 0.04, 1.9, STEEL_DK, 4)
+	mb.box(bp + Vector3(0, 1.4, 0), Vector3(1.2, 0.7, 0.06), SUN)
+	for k in 3:
+		mb.box(bp + Vector3(-0.35 + k * 0.35, 1.4, -0.04), Vector3(0.12, 0.5, 0.02), Color(0.12, 0.12, 0.14))
+	return mb.commit()
+
+
+## The bungee jump arm: a steel truss `length` m out along -z from a
+## footing at the origin, its catwalk `deck` m up, a mast and stays, a gate
+## and the rope's anchor eye at the tip. `back_y` is the ground at the stay
+## anchor 9 m behind, relative.
+static func jump_arm(length: float, deck: float, back_y: float) -> ArrayMesh:
+	var mb := MeshBuilder.new()
+	var w := 0.7 # half the catwalk's width
+	# Footing and steps up from the pad behind.
+	mb.box(Vector3(0, deck * 0.5 - 0.3, 0.6), Vector3(2.0, deck + 0.6, 2.4), CONCRETE, false)
+	for k in 3:
+		var y := deck * (k + 1) / 4.0
+		mb.box(Vector3(0, y * 0.5 - 0.2, 2.1 + (2 - k) * 0.35), Vector3(1.2, y + 0.4, 0.35), CONCRETE.darkened(0.08), false)
+	# Catwalk: grating on two side chords, cross members every 2 m.
+	mb.box(Vector3(0, deck - 0.03, -length * 0.5), Vector3(w * 2.0, 0.06, length), GRATE)
+	for s: float in [-1.0, 1.0]:
+		mb.limb(Vector3(s * w, deck - 0.12, 0.0), Vector3(s * w, deck - 0.12, -length - 0.3), 0.08, 0.08, STEEL, 4, true)
+		# Bottom chord, deeper at the root, and the truss diagonals.
+		var depth := 1.6
+		var bottom_root := Vector3(s * w * 0.6, deck - depth, 0.0)
+		var bottom_tip := Vector3(s * w * 0.6, deck - 0.5, -length)
+		mb.limb(bottom_root, bottom_tip, 0.07, 0.07, STEEL, 4, true)
+		var n := int(length / 2.0)
+		for k in n + 1:
+			var z := -length * k / n
+			var bot := bottom_root.lerp(bottom_tip, float(k) / n)
+			mb.limb(Vector3(s * w, deck - 0.12, z), bot, 0.035, 0.035, STEEL, 4, false)
+			if k < n:
+				var bot2 := bottom_root.lerp(bottom_tip, float(k + 1) / n)
+				mb.limb(Vector3(s * w, deck - 0.12, z), bot2, 0.03, 0.03, STEEL, 4, false)
+			# Handrail posts.
+			mb.limb(Vector3(s * w, deck, z), Vector3(s * w, deck + 1.05, z), 0.03, 0.03, SUN, 4, false)
+		mb.limb(Vector3(s * w, deck + 1.05, 0.0), Vector3(s * w, deck + 1.05, -length), 0.035, 0.035, SUN, 4, false)
+		mb.limb(Vector3(s * w, deck + 0.55, 0.0), Vector3(s * w, deck + 0.55, -length), 0.025, 0.025, SUN, 4, false)
+	# The mast over the footing and its stays to the arm and back to the ground.
+	# Tall enough that the stays to the tip pull at a useful angle.
+	var top := Vector3(0, deck + maxf(7.5, length * 0.32), 0.9)
+	for s: float in [-1.0, 1.0]:
+		mb.limb(Vector3(s * 0.9, deck, 1.2), top, 0.1, 0.07, STEEL, 6, true)
+	for z: float in [-length * 0.35, -length * 0.7, -length]:
+		for s: float in [-1.0, 1.0]:
+			mb.limb(top, Vector3(s * w, deck - 0.12, z), 0.025, 0.025, STEEL_DK, 3, false)
+	for s: float in [-1.0, 1.0]:
+		mb.limb(top, Vector3(s * 1.4, back_y + 0.15, 9.0), 0.025, 0.025, STEEL_DK, 3, false)
+		mb.box(Vector3(s * 1.4, back_y + 0.1, 9.0), Vector3(0.5, 0.4, 0.5), CONCRETE.darkened(0.15), false)
+	mb.box(top + Vector3(0, 0.15, 0), Vector3(0.3, 0.3, 0.3), CORAL)
+	# The gate at the tip and the anchor eye under it.
+	for s: float in [-1.0, 1.0]:
+		mb.limb(Vector3(s * w, deck, -length), Vector3(s * w, deck + 2.2, -length), 0.05, 0.05, SUN, 4, true)
+	mb.limb(Vector3(-w, deck + 2.2, -length), Vector3(w, deck + 2.2, -length), 0.05, 0.05, SUN, 4, true)
+	for k in 6:
+		mb.box(Vector3(-w + (k + 0.5) * w / 3.0, deck + 0.02, -length + 0.15), Vector3(w / 3.0, 0.02, 0.3),
+				SUN if k % 2 == 0 else Color(0.1, 0.1, 0.12))
+	mb.limb(Vector3(0, deck - 0.12, -length), Vector3(0, deck - 0.35, -length), 0.06, 0.06, STEEL_DK, 6, true)
+	# A sign at the root: coral board, sun stripes.
+	var sp := Vector3(1.6, 0.0, 2.4)
+	mb.cylinder(sp + Vector3(0, -0.2, 0), 0.05, 2.4, STEEL_DK, 4)
+	mb.box(sp + Vector3(0, 2.0, 0), Vector3(0.9, 0.6, 0.06), CORAL)
+	for k in 3:
+		mb.box(sp + Vector3(0, 1.85 + k * 0.15, -0.04), Vector3(0.7, 0.05, 0.02), SUN)
+	return mb.commit()
+
+
+## A unit rope along +y from the origin (scale y to its length).
+static func rope() -> ArrayMesh:
+	var mb := MeshBuilder.new()
+	mb.limb(Vector3.ZERO, Vector3(0, 1, 0), 0.05, 0.05, ROPE, 6, false)
+	return mb.commit()
+
+
+## A basis whose +y runs from `a` to `b` (its length is the scale).
+static func along(a: Vector3, b: Vector3) -> Basis:
+	var y := b - a
+	var l := y.length()
+	if l < 0.001:
+		return Basis.IDENTITY.scaled(Vector3(1, 0.001, 1))
+	var u := y / l
+	var x := u.cross(Vector3.FORWARD if absf(u.z) < 0.9 else Vector3.RIGHT).normalized()
+	var z := x.cross(u)
+	return Basis(x, u * l, z)
diff --git a/game/scripts/parachute.gd b/game/scripts/parachute.gd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6d6e77c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/game/scripts/parachute.gd
@@ -0,0 +1,547 @@
+extends Node
+## Parachuting (HANDOFF-air-sports.md). A bail from a helicopter MIN_HEIGHT m
+## or more over the ground free-falls, then flies a canopy down: OPEN (E) or,
+## if the player does nothing, it opens by itself at a safe height. Under the
+## canopy the stick steers, E brakes, and it flares by itself near the
+## ground. A cliff lip near BASE_NEAR is a BASE exit (E: BASE JUMP) that
+## starts the same flight. While in the air this node drives the player:
+## player.gd sets `player.air` and calls drive() each physics frame instead
+## of the walk. Lower bails keep player.gd's fall.
+##
+## main.gd: `parachute = Parachute.new(); parachute.game = self; add_child(parachute)`.
+
+const Kit = preload("res://scripts/kits/air_sports_kit.gd")
+const MeshBuilder = preload("res://scripts/mesh_builder.gd")
+const Terrain = preload("res://scripts/terrain.gd")
+const L = preload("res://scripts/layers.gd")
+const GameLog = preload("res://scripts/game_log.gd")
+const Helicopter = preload("res://scripts/helicopter.gd")
+const Tiles = preload("res://scripts/country_tiles.gd")
+
+const G := 9.8
+## Free fall: quadratic drag that settles at TERMINAL m/s.
+const TERMINAL := 50.0
+const DRAG := G / (TERMINAL * TERMINAL)
+## Lowest bail (m over the ground) that gets the canopy; lower ones fall.
+const MIN_HEIGHT := 40.0
+## Opening: OPEN_DELAY s of lines paying out (still falling), then the
+## canopy brakes the fall (OPEN_TAU s) and is fully flying INFLATE s later.
+const OPEN_DELAY := 0.6
+const OPEN_TAU := 0.6
+const INFLATE := 1.8
+## Flying: SINK m/s down, FORWARD m/s ahead, eased over FLY_TAU s; the
+## stick turns it toward where it points at TURN rad/s.
+const SINK := 5.0
+const FORWARD := 8.0
+const FLY_TAU := 0.6
+const TURN := 1.4
+## The flare under FLARE_HEIGHT m: down to FLARE_SINK and FLARE_FWD m/s.
+const FLARE_HEIGHT := 4.0
+const FLARE_SINK := 1.2
+const FLARE_FWD := 3.0
+const FLARE_TAU := 0.3
+## E under the canopy: brakes for BRAKE_TIME s (a steeper, slower glide).
+const BRAKE_TIME := 2.0
+const BRAKE_SINK := 3.0
+const BRAKE_FWD := 4.0
+## Auto-open: the full canopy wants about AUTO_CLEAR m under it.
+const AUTO_CLEAR := 32.0
+## Free fall with the stick: tracking up to TRACK m/s across the ground.
+const TRACK := 12.0
+const TRACK_ACCEL := 4.0
+## The landing hurts as player.gd's bail does: each metre of drop it equals
+## past BAIL_SAFE costs BAIL_HURT health.
+const BAIL_SAFE := 2.5
+const BAIL_HURT := 7.0
+## The BASE exit: the best cliff lip within BASE_R m of BASE_NEAR; the
+## prompt shows within BASE_REACH m of the spot behind it; the hop off is
+## EXIT_SPEED m/s out and EXIT_UP up, the canopy thrown at once.
+const BASE_NEAR := Vector2(1035.0, -2740.0)
+const BASE_R := 40.0
+const BASE_REACH := 3.0
+const EXIT_SPEED := 5.0
+const EXIT_UP := 2.0
+## The site and its marker are made when the player comes this close:
+## well before the country's tiles there build (130 m on foot, a few
+## hundred from a helicopter), so its clearing keeps them bare.
+const PREPARE_RANGE := 1200.0
+
+var game
+## Test hook: false never opens the canopy by itself.
+var auto_open := true
+## "" (on the ground), "free", "opening" or "canopy".
+var state := ""
+var player = null
+var velocity := Vector3.ZERO
+var heading := 0.0
+var bank := 0.0
+## The lowest the player came over the ground in this flight (tests).
+var min_clear := INF
+## How the last flight ended: impact (m/s into the ground), damage, where,
+## whether the canopy was flying, and the height it began at.
+var last_landing := {}
+var _t := 0.0
+var _from := 0.0
+var _brake := 0.0
+var _flare := false
+var _site := {}
+var _site_done := false
+var _prepare_tick := 0.0
+var _rig: Node3D
+var _wing: Node3D
+var _collapse := -1.0
+var _marker: MeshInstance3D
+
+
+func _ready() -> void:
+	if game == null:
+		game = get_parent()
+	add_to_group("air_sports")
+	add_to_group("parachute")
+	_rig = Node3D.new()
+	_rig.name = "Canopy"
+	_rig.physics_interpolation_mode = Node.PHYSICS_INTERPOLATION_MODE_OFF
+	_rig.visible = false
+	add_child(_rig)
+	_wing = Node3D.new()
+	_wing.position.y = Kit.RISER_Y
+	_rig.add_child(_wing)
+	var cloth := MeshInstance3D.new()
+	cloth.mesh = Kit.canopy()
+	cloth.material_override = Kit.cloth_material()
+	_wing.add_child(cloth)
+	var straps := MeshInstance3D.new()
+	straps.mesh = Kit.risers()
+	straps.material_override = MeshBuilder.material()
+	_rig.add_child(straps)
+
+
+## The ground a landing comes down on at x, z: the drawn land (the hills'
+## ground sits Terrain.drop under Terrain.height). One place, so it can
+## switch to the shared ground layer (Ground.height) later.
+static func ground_under(x: float, z: float) -> float:
+	return Terrain.height(x, z) - Terrain.drop(x, z)
+
+
+## Height over the ground at which falling at `v` m/s the canopy is fully
+## flying about AUTO_CLEAR m up.
+static func open_height(v: float) -> float:
+	return AUTO_CLEAR + v * OPEN_DELAY + maxf(v - SINK, 0.0) * OPEN_TAU
+
+
+func flying() -> bool:
+	return state != ""
+
+
+# --- Starting a flight --------------------------------------------------------
+
+## A bail from a helicopter: `p` leaves at `start` moving `v0`. True when
+## the canopy takes it (high enough, alive); false leaves player.gd's fall.
+func take_bail(p, start: Vector3, v0: Vector3) -> bool:
+	if p == null or p.dead or state != "":
+		return false
+	var h := start.y - ground_under(start.x, start.z)
+	if h < MIN_HEIGHT:
+		return false
+	_begin(p, start, v0, "free")
+	GameLog.event("bail", {"height": h, "chute": true})
+	return true
+
+
+func _begin(p, start: Vector3, v0: Vector3, first: String) -> void:
+	player = p
+	p.air = self
+	state = first
+	_t = 0.0
+	_brake = 0.0
+	_flare = false
+	_collapse = -1.0
+	velocity = v0
+	heading = p.rotation.y
+	bank = 0.0
+	p.global_position = start
+	p.reset_physics_interpolation()
+	p.velocity = Vector3.ZERO
+	p.knocked_time = 0.0
+	p.collision_layer = 0
+	p.collision_mask = L.WORLD
+	p.gesture = "hands_up"
+	_from = start.y - ground_under(start.x, start.z)
+	min_clear = _from
+	p.flies = true
+	p.above_land = _from
+	_rig.visible = first != "free"
+	_rig.scale = Vector3.ONE
+	_wing.scale = Vector3(0.12, 0.2, 0.3)
+
+
+func _open() -> void:
+	state = "opening"
+	_t = 0.0
+	_rig.visible = true
+	_wing.scale = Vector3(0.12, 0.2, 0.3)
+	heading = player.rotation.y
+	GameLog.event("chute_open", {"height": player.global_position.y - ground_under(player.global_position.x, player.global_position.z),
+			"speed": velocity.length()})
+
+
+# --- In the air ---------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## One physics frame of the flight (player.gd calls this while p.air is us).
+func drive(p, delta: float) -> void:
+	if p.dead:
+		_hand_to_fall(p)
+		return
+	_t += delta
+	var pos: Vector3 = p.global_position
+	var hag := pos.y - ground_under(pos.x, pos.z)
+	if state == "free" and (Controls.just_pressed("interact") or (auto_open and hag <= open_height(-velocity.y))):
+		_open()
+	var stick := Controls.world_move()
+	stick.y = 0.0
+	if state == "free" or (state == "opening" and _t < OPEN_DELAY):
+		_fall_step(stick, delta)
+	else:
+		_canopy_step(stick, hag, delta)
+	_pose(p, stick, delta)
+	_move(p, delta)
+
+
+func _fall_step(stick: Vector3, delta: float) -> void:
+	velocity.y -= G * delta
+	velocity -= velocity * velocity.length() * DRAG * delta
+	if state == "free" and stick.length_squared() > 0.04:
+		var flat := Vector3(velocity.x, 0.0, velocity.z).move_toward(stick.limit_length(1.0) * TRACK, TRACK_ACCEL * delta)
+		velocity.x = flat.x
+		velocity.z = flat.z
+
+
+func _canopy_step(stick: Vector3, hag: float, delta: float) -> void:
+	if state == "opening" and _t >= OPEN_DELAY + INFLATE:
+		state = "canopy"
+	var turn := 0.0
+	if stick.length_squared() > 0.04:
+		var want := atan2(-stick.x, -stick.z)
+		var diff := angle_difference(heading, want)
+		turn = clampf(diff * 2.0, -TURN, TURN)
+		heading = wrapf(heading + turn * delta, -PI, PI)
+	bank = lerpf(bank, turn * 0.3, 1.0 - exp(-4.0 * delta))
+	if Controls.just_pressed("interact"):
+		_brake = BRAKE_TIME
+	_brake = maxf(_brake - delta, 0.0)
+	if _flare and hag > FLARE_HEIGHT + 4.0:
+		_flare = false # flown off a lip or over a dip: the full glide again
+	elif not _flare and hag < FLARE_HEIGHT and velocity.y < 0.0 and (state == "canopy" or _t > OPEN_DELAY + 0.5):
+		_flare = true
+	var sink := SINK
+	var fwd := FORWARD
+	var tau := FLY_TAU if state == "canopy" else OPEN_TAU
+	if _flare:
+		sink = FLARE_SINK
+		fwd = FLARE_FWD
+		tau = FLARE_TAU
+	elif _brake > 0.0:
+		sink = BRAKE_SINK
+		fwd = BRAKE_FWD
+	var ahead := Vector3(-sin(heading), 0.0, -cos(heading))
+	var want_v := ahead * fwd + Vector3.DOWN * sink
+	velocity += (want_v - velocity) * (1.0 - exp(-delta / tau))
+
+
+## Belly to earth in free fall (facing where the stick tracks), upright
+## under the canopy, banked into its turns.
+func _pose(p, stick: Vector3, delta: float) -> void:
+	var falling := state == "free"
+	var k := 1.0 - exp(-5.0 * delta)
+	p.rotation.x = lerpf(p.rotation.x, -PI * 0.5 if falling else 0.0, k)
+	if falling:
+		if stick.length_squared() > 0.04:
+			p.rotation.y = lerp_angle(p.rotation.y, atan2(-stick.x, -stick.z), 1.0 - exp(-3.0 * delta))
+		p.rotation.z = lerpf(p.rotation.z, 0.0, k)
+		heading = p.rotation.y
+	else:
+		p.rotation.y = lerp_angle(p.rotation.y, heading, k)
+		p.rotation.z = lerpf(p.rotation.z, bank, k)
+
+
+func _move(p, delta: float) -> void:
+	var col: KinematicCollision3D = p.move_and_collide(velocity * delta)
+	if col != null:
+		var n := col.get_normal()
+		if n.y > 0.6:
+			_land(p, true) # on a roof: down to open ground beside it
+			return
+		# A wall: slide along it.
+		velocity = velocity.slide(n)
+		p.move_and_collide(col.get_remainder().slide(n))
+	var pos: Vector3 = p.global_position
+	var g := ground_under(pos.x, pos.z)
+	if pos.y <= g:
+		p.global_position.y = g
+		if velocity.y <= 0.0:
+			_land(p, false)
+			return
+		velocity.y = 0.0
+	var clear: float = p.global_position.y - g
+	min_clear = minf(min_clear, clear)
+	p.above_land = clear
+
+
+# --- Down ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+func _land(p, roof: bool) -> void:
+	var pos: Vector3 = p.global_position
+	var n := Vector3.UP if roof else Terrain.normal(pos.x, pos.z)
+	var impact := maxf(-velocity.dot(n), 0.0)
+	var canopy := state != "free"
+	var damage := 0.0
+	if canopy:
+		var drop := impact * impact / (2.0 * G)
+		damage = maxf(drop - BAIL_SAFE, 0.0) * BAIL_HURT
+	else:
+		damage = maxf(_from - BAIL_SAFE, 0.0) * BAIL_HURT # as player.gd's bail
+	_release(p)
+	if roof or _wet(pos, ground_under(pos.x, pos.z)):
+		pos = _open_ground_near(pos)
+	pos.y = ground_under(pos.x, pos.z)
+	p.global_position = pos
+	p.reset_physics_interpolation()
+	last_landing = {"impact": impact, "damage": damage, "pos": pos, "canopy": canopy, "from": _from, "roof": roof}
+	if canopy:
+		GameLog.event("chute_landed", {"impact": impact, "damage": damage, "from": _from})
+		if damage > 0.0:
+			p.knock_down(1.2 + minf(damage * 0.03, 2.0))
+			p.take_hit(null, damage, Vector3.ZERO)
+		elif impact > 2.5:
+			p.play_action("stumble")
+		_collapse = 0.0
+		_rig.global_position = pos
+	else:
+		GameLog.event("bail_landed", {"from": _from})
+		p.knock_down(1.2)
+		p.take_hit(null, damage, Vector3.ZERO)
+		Fx.crash(pos, impact, true)
+		_rig.visible = false
+
+
+## Back on its feet: the walk takes over again.
+func _release(p) -> void:
+	state = ""
+	player = null
+	p.air = null
+	p.flies = false
+	p.above_land = 0.0
+	p.gesture = ""
+	p.rotation.x = 0.0
+	p.rotation.z = 0.0
+	p.velocity = Vector3.ZERO
+	if not p.dead:
+		p._set_standing_layers()
+	# The ground's draw drop is looked up afresh where they land.
+	p.set("_drop_at", Vector2.INF)
+
+
+## Killed in the air: player.gd's fall takes the body down.
+func _hand_to_fall(p) -> void:
+	var pos: Vector3 = p.global_position
+	var h := maxf(pos.y - ground_under(pos.x, pos.z), 0.0)
+	_release(p)
+	_rig.visible = false
+	p._fall = h
+	p._fall_v = maxf(-velocity.y, 0.0)
+	p._fall_from = h
+
+
+## Ends a flight at once, unhurt (a mission replay or respawn moves the
+## player; player.gd calls this from stand_at and respawn).
+func cancel() -> void:
+	if player != null:
+		_release(player)
+	state = ""
+	_rig.visible = false
+	_collapse = -1.0
+
+
+func _wet(p: Vector3, g: float) -> bool:
+	var city = game.get("city") if game != null else null
+	var plan = city.plan if city != null else null
+	var q := Vector2(p.x, p.z)
+	if Helicopter._wet(plan, q, g):
+		return true
+	var country = city.get("country") if city != null else null
+	return country != null and not country.lakes.is_empty() and not country.lake_at(q).is_empty()
+
+
+## The nearest open, dry ground to `p` (no roof over it), rings out to 80 m.
+func _open_ground_near(p: Vector3) -> Vector3:
+	if not is_inside_tree():
+		return p
+	var space := get_viewport().find_world_3d().direct_space_state
+	for r: float in [0.0, 6.0, 12.0, 20.0, 30.0, 45.0, 60.0, 80.0]:
+		for k in (1 if r == 0.0 else 12):
+			var q := p + Vector3(r, 0.0, 0.0).rotated(Vector3.UP, TAU * k / 12.0)
+			var g := ground_under(q.x, q.z)
+			if _wet(q, g):
+				continue
+			var ray := PhysicsRayQueryParameters3D.create(Vector3(q.x, g + 200.0, q.z), Vector3(q.x, g - 0.5, q.z), L.WORLD)
+			var hit := space.intersect_ray(ray)
+			if hit.is_empty() or float(hit.position.y) <= g + 1.0:
+				return Vector3(q.x, g, q.z)
+	return p
+
+
+# --- Drawing ------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+func _process(delta: float) -> void:
+	_prepare_tick -= delta
+	if not _site_done and _prepare_tick <= 0.0:
+		_prepare_tick = 0.5
+		var p = game.get("player") if game != null else null
+		if p != null and Vector2(p.global_position.x, p.global_position.z).distance_to(BASE_NEAR) < PREPARE_RANGE:
+			base_site()
+	if player != null and state != "":
+		var xf: Transform3D = player.get_global_transform_interpolated()
+		_rig.global_transform = Transform3D(Basis.from_euler(Vector3(0.0, heading, bank)), xf.origin)
+		if state != "free":
+			var k := smoothstep(0.0, 1.0, clampf((_t - 0.15) / (OPEN_DELAY + INFLATE - 0.15), 0.0, 1.0))
+			_wing.scale = Vector3(lerpf(0.12, 1.0, k), lerpf(0.2, 1.0, k), lerpf(0.3, 1.0, k))
+	elif _collapse >= 0.0:
+		# Down: the canopy settles onto the ground behind and is packed away.
+		_collapse += delta
+		var k := clampf(_collapse / 1.4, 0.0, 1.0)
+		_rig.scale = Vector3(1.0, lerpf(1.0, 0.06, k), 1.0)
+		if _collapse > 4.0:
+			_rig.visible = false
+			_rig.scale = Vector3.ONE
+			_collapse = -1.0
+
+
+# --- The BASE exit ------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## The BASE exit: {lip, dir (out over the drop), stand (where to stand,
+## a metre behind the lip), drop (m down 64 m out)}, found once from the
+## terrain; {} if there is none.
+func base_site() -> Dictionary:
+	if _site_done:
+		return _site
+	_site_done = true
+	if Terrain.nx == 0:
+		return _site
+	var best := [-INF, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
+	var x := BASE_NEAR.x - BASE_R
+	while x <= BASE_NEAR.x + BASE_R:
+		var z := BASE_NEAR.y - BASE_R
+		while z <= BASE_NEAR.y + BASE_R:
+			if Vector2(x, z).distance_to(BASE_NEAR) <= BASE_R:
+				for a in 32:
+					var ang := TAU * a / 32.0
+					var s := _lip_score(x, z, ang)
+					if s > best[0]:
+						best = [s, x, z, ang]
+			z += 4.0
+		x += 4.0
+	if best[0] == -INF:
+		return _site
+	var bx: float = best[1]
+	var bz: float = best[2]
+	var ba: float = best[3]
+	for i in range(-3, 4):
+		for j in range(-3, 4):
+			for k in range(-4, 5):
+				var ang := ba + deg_to_rad(2.0 * k)
+				var s := _lip_score(bx + i, bz + j, ang)
+				if s > best[0]:
+					best = [s, bx + i, bz + j, ang]
+	var px: float = best[1]
+	var pz: float = best[2]
+	var dir := Vector3(cos(best[3]), 0.0, sin(best[3]))
+	var top := Terrain.height(px, pz)
+	# The lip: out along the drop while the ground keeps within 0.6 m of the top.
+	var out := 0.0
+	while out < 12.0 and absf(Terrain.height(px + dir.x * (out + 0.25), pz + dir.z * (out + 0.25)) - top) <= 0.6:
+		out += 0.25
+	var lip := Vector3(px + dir.x * out, 0.0, pz + dir.z * out)
+	lip.y = Terrain.height(lip.x, lip.z)
+	var stand := lip - dir * 1.0
+	stand.y = ground_under(stand.x, stand.z)
+	_site = {"lip": lip, "dir": dir, "stand": stand,
+			"drop": top - Terrain.height(lip.x + dir.x * 64.0, lip.z + dir.z * 64.0)}
+	_build_marker()
+	return _site
+
+
+## How good a jump off (x, z) toward `ang` is, or -INF: level ground behind,
+## and the land falling away at least 8 m in 8 m, 20 in 16 and 45 in 64.
+static func _lip_score(x: float, z: float, ang: float) -> float:
+	var dx := cos(ang)
+	var dz := sin(ang)
+	var g0 := Terrain.height(x, z)
+	if absf(Terrain.height(x - dx * 2.0, z - dz * 2.0) - g0) > 0.8 or Terrain.normal(x - dx * 4.0, z - dz * 4.0).y < 0.85:
+		return -INF
+	var d8 := g0 - Terrain.height(x + dx * 8.0, z + dz * 8.0)
+	if d8 < 8.0:
+		return -INF
+	var d16 := g0 - Terrain.height(x + dx * 16.0, z + dz * 16.0)
+	if d16 < 20.0:
+		return -INF
+	var d64 := g0 - Terrain.height(x + dx * 64.0, z + dz * 64.0)
+	if d64 < 45.0:
+		return -INF
+	return d16 + 0.3 * d64
+
+
+func _build_marker() -> void:
+	var lip: Vector3 = _site.lip
+	var dir: Vector3 = _site.dir
+	var back := lip - dir * 2.0
+	_marker = MeshInstance3D.new()
+	_marker.name = "BaseExit"
+	_marker.mesh = Kit.base_exit(Terrain.height(back.x, back.z) - lip.y)
+	_marker.material_override = MeshBuilder.material()
+	add_child(_marker)
+	_marker.global_transform = Transform3D(Basis(Vector3.UP, atan2(-dir.x, -dir.z)), lip)
+	# No trees or stones on the exit.
+	Tiles.clearings.append([Vector2(lip.x, lip.z), 0.0, Vector2(5.0, 5.0)])
+
+
+func _at_lip() -> bool:
+	var p = game.get("player") if game != null else null
+	if p == null or p.vehicle != null or p.dead or p.knocked_time > 0.0 or p.air != null or not p.controllable:
+		return false
+	if Vector2(p.global_position.x, p.global_position.z).distance_to(BASE_NEAR) > BASE_R + 20.0:
+		return false
+	var s := base_site()
+	if s.is_empty():
+		return false
+	var at: Vector3 = s.stand
+	return Vector2(p.global_position.x - at.x, p.global_position.z - at.z).length() <= BASE_REACH
+
+
+# --- The HUD and E ------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## [text, button] for the HUD: the flight's height and what E does, or the
+## BASE exit's offer at the lip; [] otherwise.
+func prompt() -> Array:
+	if state != "" and player != null:
+		var alt := roundi(maxf(player.above_land, 0.0))
+		if state == "free":
+			return ["Free fall   ALT %d m   Open: E / OPEN" % alt, "OPEN"]
+		return ["Canopy   ALT %d m   Steer with the stick   Brake: E" % alt, "BRAKE"]
+	if _at_lip():
+		return ["E: BASE JUMP", "JUMP"]
+	return []
+
+
+## Off the lip, when the player stands at it. True when it jumped.
+func try_interact() -> bool:
+	if state != "" or not _at_lip():
+		return false
+	var p = game.player
+	var dir: Vector3 = _site.dir
+	p.rotation.y = atan2(-dir.x, -dir.z)
+	var start: Vector3 = _site.stand
+	start.y += 0.05
+	_begin(p, start, dir * EXIT_SPEED + Vector3.UP * EXIT_UP, "opening")
+	_from = _site.drop
+	GameLog.event("base_jump", {"at": start, "drop": _site.drop})
+	return true
